/// The platform, its transcript and its collections namespace are values
/// (§3.1.1): stateless but for what the module they belong to was handed,
/// so any two of a kind are equal and, a value having no identity,
/// identical. Each is an instance of its own class, so none answers
/// another's protocol (which `crates/ns-runtime/tests/representation.rs`
/// checks, a program being unable to ask another object for its class).
/// The platform's class, `platform Platform`, answers `new`: what holds the
/// VM mirror is the `PlatformFactory` instance enclosing it, which no
/// program is handed, so a second platform is as harmless as the first.
class PlatformValues = Object new () (
  public main: platform args: arguments = (
    |
      t
      c
    |
    t:: platform transcript.
    c:: platform collections.
    t
        show: (t == platform transcript) printString;
        newLine.
    t
        show: (t = platform Transcript new) printString;
        newLine.
    t
        show: (platform = platform Platform new) printString;
        newLine.
    t
        show: (platform hash = platform Platform new hash) printString;
        newLine.
    t
        show: (c List == platform Platform new collections List) printString;
        newLine.
  )
)
